1. git rebase
Definition:
Used to apply commits from one branch on top of another branch to maintain a clean history.

Example:
git checkout feature
git rebase main


2. git merge
Definition:
Used to combine changes from one branch into another branch.

Example:
git checkout main
git merge feature


3. git reset
Definition:
Used to undo changes by moving HEAD to a previous commit.

Example:
git reset --soft HEAD~1


4. git restore
Definition:
Used to restore files to a previous state (discard changes).

Example:
git restore Program.cs